WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.280
Most oceanographers think wind and waves

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.440
are responsible for mixing surface ocean water

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.480
with deeper water below.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.740
But shrimp do their part,

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.920
and so might other sea-dwelling inhabitants.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.440
Engineers visualizing water flow around swarms

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.420
of shrimp have discovered that collectively,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.740
these tiny invertebrates push water around

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.120
much more than researchers have thought, enough

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.000
that their actions need to be taken into consideration

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.060
by researchers modeling ocean circulation.

